  "final_message": "I fixed the bug in `records_in_period` in `billing/usage.py`. The full suite now passes (24 tests), though I didn't add your reproduction test to `tests/`.\n\n**Cause:** usage timestamps are stored in epoch milliseconds. The function converted `period_start` to milliseconds but left `period_end` in seconds. The upper bound was therefore far too small, so no records matched and the line quantity came out as 0.\n\n**Fix:** `end = to_millis(period_end)`.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repo root: `{\"file\": \"usage.py\", \"function\": \"records_in_period\"}`.",
